ries":["Tree","Breadth-First Search"],"constraintBlocks":[],"contentBlocks":[{"sequence":0,"text":"You are given an integer array `parent` of length `n` representing a rooted tree with nodes labeled from 0 to `n - 1`.\n\nThe tree is **rooted** at node 0, so `parent[0] = -1`. For each node `i` where `1 <= i <= n - 1`, `parent[i]` denotes the parent of node `i`.\n\nYou are also given an integer array `nums` of length `n`, where `nums[i]` denotes the value of node `i`.\n\nThe weight of a node `i` at depth `d` is `nums[i] * (h - d + 1)`, where `h` is the height of the tree.\n\nReturn the **sum** of the weights of all nodes in the tree.\n\nThe **depth** of a node is the number of nodes on the path from the root to that node, inclusive, with the root having depth 1.\n\nThe **height** of the tree is the maximum depth among all nodes in the tree.\n\n**Example 1:**","type":"text"},{"alt":"Problem image","contentType":"image/png","localPath":"leetcode_seed/assets/problems/4015-weighted-sum-of-a-tree/4015-t1.png","sequence":1,"sha256":"a236fcf08cf80aacf3927cc3c906c85849182358fc66d41a821be2eaf4bcbbd5","type":"image"},{"sequence":2,"text":"**Input:** parent = [-1,0,0,0,2,2], nums = [5,2,3,1,4,6]\n\n**Output:** 37\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nThe height of the tree is 3.\n\n| Node | `nums[i]` | Depth (`d`) | Weight |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 0 | 5 | 1 | `5 * (3 - 1 + 1) = 15` |\n| 1 | 2 | 2 | `2 * (3 - 2 + 1) = 4` |\n| 2 | 3 | 2 | `3 * (3 - 2 + 1) = 6` |\n| 3 | 1 | 2 | `1 * (3 - 2 + 1) = 2` |\n| 4 | 4 | 3 | `4 * (3 - 3 + 1) = 4` |\n| 5 | 6 | 3 | `6 * (3 - 3 + 1) = 6` |\n\nThe sum of all node weights is `15 + 4 + 6 + 2 + 4 + 6 = 37`.\n\n**Example 2:**","type":"text"},{"alt":"Problem image","contentType":"image/png","localPath":"leetcode_seed/assets/problems/4015-weighted-sum-of-a-tree/4015-t2.png","sequence":3,"sha256":"79d819d75a593a6c9308456d5161c50b552b1f0454b94031f705a9941427cc3a","type":"image"},{"sequence":4,"text":"**Input:** parent = [-1,0,1,2], nums = [1,2,3,4]\n\n**Output:** 20\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nThe height of the tree is 4.\n\n| Node | `nums[i]` | Depth (`d`) | Weight |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 0 | 1 | 1 | `1 * (4 - 1 + 1) = 4` |\n| 1 | 2 | 2 | `2 * (4 - 2 + 1) = 6` |\n| 2 | 3 | 3 | `3 * (4 - 3 + 1) = 6` |\n| 3 | 4 | 4 | `4 * (4 - 4 + 1) = 4` |\n\nThe sum of all node weights is `4 + 6 + 6 + 4 = 20`.\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n- `1 <= n <= 10⁵`\n\n- `n == parent.length == nums.length`\n\n- `parent[0] == -1`\n\n- `0 <= parent[i] <= n - 1` for all `i` in `[1, n - 1]`\n\n- `1 <= nums[i] <= 10⁶`\n\n- The input is generated such that the array `parent` represents a valid tree rooted at node 0.","type":"text"}],"contentHtml":"","contentHtmlLocal":"","databaseEntry":{"categories":["Tree","Breadth-First Search"],"createdAt":0,"difficulty":"Medium","lastRevisionAt":0,"problem":"You are given an integer array `parent` of length `n` representing a rooted tree with nodes labeled from 0 to `n - 1`.\n\nThe tree is **rooted** at node 0, so `parent[0] = -1`. For each node `i` where `1 <= i <= n - 1`, `parent[i]` denotes the parent of node `i`.\n\nYou are also given an integer array `nums` of length `n`, where `nums[i]` denotes the value of node `i`.\n\nThe weight of a node `i` at depth `d` is `nums[i] * (h - d + 1)`, where `h` is the height of the tree.\n\nReturn the **sum** of the weights of all nodes in the tree.\n\nThe **depth** of a node is the number of nodes on the path from the root to that node, inclusive, with the root having depth 1.\n\nThe **height** of the tree is the maximum depth among all nodes in the tree.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n[[img:leetcode_seed/assets/problems/4015-weighted-sum-of-a-tree/4015-t1.png]]\n\n**Input:** parent = [-1,0,0,0,2,2], nums = [5,2,3,1,4,6]\n\n**Output:** 37\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nThe height of the tree is 3.\n\n| Node | `nums[i]` | Depth (`d`) | Weight |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 0 | 5 | 1 | `5 * (3 - 1 + 1) = 15` |\n| 1 | 2 | 2 | `2 * (3 - 2 + 1) = 4` |\n| 2 | 3 | 2 | `3 * (3 - 2 + 1) = 6` |\n| 3 | 1 | 2 | `1 * (3 - 2 + 1) = 2` |\n| 4 | 4 | 3 | `4 * (3 - 3 + 1) = 4` |\n| 5 | 6 | 3 | `6 * (3 - 3 + 1) = 6` |\n\nThe sum of all node weights is `15 + 4 + 6 + 2 + 4 + 6 = 37`.\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n[[img:leetcode_seed/assets/problems/4015-weighted-sum-of-a-tree/4015-t2.png]]\n\n**Input:** parent = [-1,0,1,2], nums = [1,2,3,4]\n\n**Output:** 20\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nThe height of the tree is 4.\n\n| Node | `nums[i]` | Depth (`d`) | Weight |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 0 | 1 | 1 | `1 * (4 - 1 + 1) = 4` |\n| 1 | 2 | 2 | `2 * (4 - 2 + 1) = 6` |\n| 2 | 3 | 3 | `3 * (4 - 3 + 1) = 6` |\n| 3 | 4 | 4 | `4 * (4 - 4 + 1) = 4` |\n\nThe sum of all node weights is `4 + 6 + 6 + 4 = 20`.\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n- `1 <= n <= 10⁵`\n\n- `n == parent.length == nums.length`\n\n- `parent[0] == -1`\n\n- `0 <= parent[i] <= n - 1` for all `i` in `[1, n - 1]`\n\n- `1 <= nums[i] <= 10⁶`\n\n- The input is generated such that the array `parent` represents a valid tree rooted at node 0.","problemLink":"https://leetcode.com/problems/weighted-sum-of-a-tree/","problemName":"Weighted Sum of a Tree","problemNumber":4015,"revisionAnchorAt":0,"revisionCount":0,"revisionDates":[],"revisionPlanHours":[1,24,168,336,672],"solutionCode":"","testCases":"","updatedAt":0},"descriptionBlocks":[{"sequence":0,"text":"You are given an integer array `parent` of length `n` representing a rooted tree with nodes labeled from 0 to `n - 1`.\n\nThe tree is **rooted** at node 0, so `parent[0] = -1`. For each node `i` where `1 <= i <= n - 1`, `parent[i]` denotes the parent of node `i`.\n\nYou are also given an integer array `nums` of length `n`, where `nums[i]` denotes the value of node `i`.\n\nThe weight of a node `i` at depth `d` is `nums[i] * (h - d + 1)`, where `h` is the height of the tree.\n\nReturn the **sum** of the weights of all nodes in the tree.\n\nThe **depth** of a node is the number of nodes on the path from the root to that node, inclusive, with the root having depth 1.\n\nThe **height** of the tree is the m